End user checklist
The end user needs:
Local admin rights on the server.
The QualysCloudAgent.exe installer.
The correct:
CustomerId
ActivationId
WebServiceUri
Internet/proxy access from the server to Qualys over HTTPS/443.
PowerShell or Command Prompt opened as Administrator.
 
Folder requirement?
No special folder is required.
The command only needs to match where the installer is located.
Example if the installer is here:``` text
D:\Tools\QualysCloudAgent.exe
```

Then the command should start with:``` powershell
D:\Tools\QualysCloudAgent.exe
```

Example:``` powershell
D:\Tools\QualysCloudAgent.exe CustomerId="{YOUR-CUSTOMER-ID}" ActivationId="{YOUR-ACTIVATION-ID}" WebServiceUri="https://<your-qualys-platform-url>/CloudAgent" /quiet
```

 
Short answer
Yes, the installer must be on the server or reachable by the server.
No, it does not need to be in a certain folder.
The user just needs to run the command using the correct path to the installer.
